## Firmware Audit Results

### Hardware Pinout — Confirmed Changes

> [!IMPORTANT]
> User confirmed: **PZEM integration is completely removed.** All UART pins for PZEM are freed.

| Pin | HTML Model Usage | Post-Audit Usage |
|-----|-----------------|------------------|
| GPIO 16 | PZEM-A RX (UART2) | **Freed — unused** |
| GPIO 17 | PZEM-A TX (UART2) | **Freed — unused** |
| GPIO 5 | PZEM-B RX (UART1) | **Freed — unused** |
| GPIO 4 | PZEM-B TX (UART1) | **Freed — unused** |
| GPIO 18 | PZEM-C RX (SoftSerial/UART0) ⚠️ | **Freed — unused** |
| GPIO 19 | PZEM-C TX (SoftSerial/UART0) ⚠️ | **Freed — unused** |
| GPIO 21 | DS3231 SDA (I²C) | **Retained — RTC** |
| GPIO 22 | DS3231 SCL (I²C) | **Retained — RTC** |
| GPIO 25 | Relay OUT (Active HIGH) | **Retained — Load relay** |
| GPIO 1 | TX0 (USB debug UART) | **Retained for debug** |
| GPIO 3 | RX0 (USB debug UART) | **Retained for debug** |

> [!WARNING]
> The original model used GPIO 18/19 for PZEM-C via SoftSerial sharing UART0. This would have **conflicted** with USB debug serial on GPIO 1/3 during flash/reset cycles. Since PZEM is now removed, this conflict is eliminated entirely.

> [!NOTE]
> GPIO 0 must still float during boot (boot mode). GPIO 25 relay init must be `HIGH` (CLOSED) at boot to maintain default feeding state.

### Firmware Logic Retained (simplified)

```cpp
void setup() {
  Serial.begin(115200);           // debug
  Wire.begin(21, 22);             // DS3231 RTC
  if (!rtc.begin()) halt("RTC not found");
  pinMode(25, OUTPUT);
  digitalWrite(25, HIGH);          // relay CLOSED at boot
  connectWiFi();
  syncNTP();
  connectWebSocket();              // CMD_RELAY_ON / CMD_RELAY_OFF listener
}

void loop() {
  // Every 5s: build minimal payload (device_id, ts, relay_state) → POST /api/ingest
  if (millis() - lastPost >= 5000) {
    String payload = buildPayload();   // no PZEM fields
    sendTelemetry(payload);
    lastPost = millis();
  }
  wsClient.loop();                   // process relay commands
}
```

### Firmware Logic Removed
- All `PZEM004Tv30` library calls and objects (`pzemA`, `pzemB`, `pzemC`)
- All `Serial1.begin()` / `Serial2.begin()` / `pzemC.begin()` UART inits
- `safetyCheck()` overvoltage/blackout trip (no sensor to read voltage from)
- Phase voltage/current/watts/kWh/PF/frequency fields in JSON payload

