## Proposed Changes

### 1. Database Schema

#### [MODIFY] [schema.prisma](file:///c:/Users/Client/CApstone/OptiFeed/apps/web/prisma/schema.prisma)
Add two new models:

```prisma
model EnergyDevice {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  mac         String   @unique  // ESP32 MAC address (device_id)
  token       String   @unique  // X-Device-Token
  label       String            // e.g. "CICT Building A"
  pondId      String?           // optional link to Pond
  relayState  Boolean  @default(true)  // current commanded relay state
  lastSeenAt  DateTime?
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())

  pond     Pond?          @relation(fields: [pondId], references: [id])
  readings EnergyReading[]
}

model EnergyReading {
  id           String   @id @default(cuid())
  deviceId     String
  timestamp    DateTime
  relayState   Boolean
  createdAt    DateTime @default(now())

  device EnergyDevice @relation(fields: [deviceId], references: [id])

  @@index([deviceId, timestamp])
}
```

> [!NOTE]
> `EnergyReading` stores only relay state + timestamp (no PZEM phase data) since PZEM is removed. The index on `(deviceId, timestamp)` keeps the 5s-interval telemetry queries fast.

