### 2. API Ingest Route

#### [NEW] [route.ts](file:///c:/Users/Client/CApstone/OptiFeed/apps/web/app/api/ingest/route.ts)

A Next.js Route Handler:
- `POST /api/ingest`
- Auth: validates `X-Device-Token` header against `EnergyDevice.token` in DB
- Zod schema validation of the minimal JSON payload:
  ```json
  {
    "device_id": "A4:CF:12:7E:3B:09",
    "timestamp": "2026-07-10T15:00:00+08:00",
    "relay_state": true
  }
  ```
- On success: upsert `EnergyDevice.lastSeenAt`, create `EnergyReading`, return `204 No Content`
- Rate limit: 1 req/s per device (checked via `lastSeenAt`)
- Errors: `401` for bad token, `429` for rate limit, `422` for Zod failure

