### 3. Relay State API (for ESP32 polling)

#### [NEW] [route.ts](file:///c:/Users/Client/CApstone/OptiFeed/apps/web/app/api/relay-state/route.ts)

A simple `GET /api/relay-state?device_id=<MAC>` endpoint:
- Validates `X-Device-Token` header
- Returns `{ "relay_state": true }` (current commanded state from `EnergyDevice.relayState`)
- The ESP32 polls this every 5s alongside its POST cycle as an alternative to raw WebSocket

> [!NOTE]
> This is a Supabase Realtime-free fallback. The ESP32's existing `wsLoop()` WebSocket code handles real-time relay commands when WS is available. The polling endpoint is a fallback / simpler bootstrap path.

